      "name": "Certificate file upload",
      "steps": ["administrator selects an allowed file", "multipart request reaches certificate controller", "file streams to an opaque date-partitioned R2 object key", "certificate row references the key", "upload audit records filename, uploader, competent person, and time", "downloads return a five-minute signed URL"]
    },
    {
      "name": "Certificate and routine-maintenance notifications",
      "steps": ["startup run, daily cron, manual scheduler call, or working-hour threshold triggers a scan", "candidate and tier are calculated", "transaction claims a NotificationDelivery idempotency key", "River email and/or ClickUp job is inserted in the same transaction", "worker calls SMTP or ClickUp", "delivery is marked SENT or attempt/final failure is recorded", "scheduler pages read the audit and failures"]
